  "evaluation": "All three correctly classify the disagreement as genuine and identify population as the strongest explanation: pregnancy-related postpartum depression versus depression in elderly adults. B is the most precise and restrained, clearly distinguishing measured serum vitamin D from dietary intake. A is similarly sound and additionally notes the differing reference comparisons. C reaches the same correct judgment, but its characterization of the PHQ-9 cutoff as “lenient” adds an unnecessary interpretation not supplied by the fields. None of the studies provides a basis for calling the disagreement apparent.",
  "ranking": ["B", "A", "C"]
}
